WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:00.960
(audience laughing)

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.350
- [Ross] Hey Gunther, you
got stairs in your place.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.213
- Yeah.
- Yeah, go nuts.

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.260
(audience laughs)

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.450
- Rachel?

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.760
- Yeah.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.180
- I know you're leaving tonight,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.373
but I just have to tell you.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.426
I love you.

00:00:18.426 --> 00:00:20.300
(audience laughs)

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.309
- Mike hit my mom with a car.

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:25.660
(audience laughs)

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.493
- No, I didn't.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.890
Seriously, you wanna make one of those?

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.960
- One, how about a whole bunch?

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.160
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.730
Oh we can teach them to sing

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.504
and we can be like the von Trapp family.

00:00:35.504 --> 00:00:36.380
(audience laughs)

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.250
- Hey Janice.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.670
- Oh my God, I am so glad you called me.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.100
I had the most supremely awful day.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.323
- Oh my--
- Yeah yeah yeah.

00:00:45.323 --> 00:00:48.979
(audience laughs)

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:52.859
I must have you Janice
Litman-Goralnik, nee Hosenstein.

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:55.692
(audience laughs)

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.060
- Chandler, what are you talking about?

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.563
- Martha Ludwin's daughter
is gonna call you.

00:01:05.096 --> 00:01:08.440
Mmm, what's that curry taste?

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.136
Curry.
(audience laughs)

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:12.376
Mmm.

00:01:12.376 --> 00:01:14.185
(audience laughs)

00:01:14.185 --> 00:01:16.970
- I think they're great, I really do.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.613
- Do you remember the Ludwins?

00:01:18.613 --> 00:01:20.500
The big one had a thing
for you, didn't she?

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.540
- They all had a thing for him.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.150
- We better get going, it's late.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.210
Jack's not allowed to
drive at night anymore,

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.000
he has trouble staying in his lane.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.090
- The last winter I went
up on a church's lawn

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.120
and drove right through a manger scene.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.011
The papers thought it was a hate crime.

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.540
(audience laughs)

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.870
- Anyway, it was lovely seeing you.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.230
- Oh there's the waitress.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.210
Excuse me, miss.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.170
Hello, miss?

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.003
- It's Phoebe.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.080
Hi.
- Hey.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.740
- Hi.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.920
Okay, will that be all?

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.070
(audience laughs)

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:47.920
We really better get going.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.910
- Oh right, you have a
church group meeting tonight.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:50.843
- Right.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:54.169
(audience laughs)

00:01:54.169 --> 00:01:55.270
- Hello.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.615
(audience laughs)

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:57.919
- [Emily] Hello.
(Monica screeches)

00:01:57.919 --> 00:01:59.225
(audience laughs)

00:01:59.225 --> 00:02:00.164
(Rachel shrieks in excitement)

00:02:00.164 --> 00:02:01.750
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.090
- Emily?

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:03.923
- Yes.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.381
- I'm Rachel Green.

00:02:05.381 --> 00:02:07.130
- Thank goodness.
- Yeah.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.410
There has been tiny, tiny change of plans.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.210
Turns out I'm not free tonight, so--

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.686
- Really?

00:02:12.686 --> 00:02:15.100
(chuckles) Well, that's
just lovely, isn't it?

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.150
I must have missed your call,

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.690
even though I didn't
leave the flat all day.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:19.333
Are you thinking about me?

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.570
No, of course you're not.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.820
But if you are, call me tonight.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:24.683
Okay, bye.

00:02:26.057 --> 00:02:27.080
(answering machine beeps)

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.249
- No!

00:02:28.249 --> 00:02:29.330
(audience laughs)

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.470
- Oh hey hey, I got that.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.420
- Oh, thanks sweetie.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.624
- No problem.

00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:37.124
♪ All my life ♪

00:02:37.997 --> 00:02:40.590
- I cannot wait for
you to meet my friends.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:41.825
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:02:41.825 --> 00:02:43.400
- You don't think they'll
judge and ridicule me?

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.434
- No no, they will, I just...

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.600
- Can't wait.
- Can't wait. (laughs)

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.340
Come on, they're gonna love you.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.637
- Hey.

00:02:49.637 --> 00:02:50.910
- Hey Julie.
- Julie.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.070
Hey, how are you doing?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.600
- Oh, oh I don't know.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.870
I mean, it's definitely
weird not being with Ross,

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.420
but I guess I'm doing okay.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.770
Actually, I've got some
of his stuff that he...

00:03:02.479 --> 00:03:04.520
(orchestral music)

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.353
(audience laughs)

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.844
- It's James Bond.

00:03:11.844 --> 00:03:14.160
(audience laughs)

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.090
- Sorry we're late.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.390
- That's okay, come on in.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.520
I'm sorry, is Monica Geller coming?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.700
I was told she was.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.730
- Dr. Burke, it's me.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.210
- Monica?

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.223
If you do get her,

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.073
don't let her go.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:29.943
Trust me.

00:03:33.376 --> 00:03:35.770
- You know, Richard, you are a good guy.

00:03:37.538 --> 00:03:39.310
(audience laughs)

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.238
- I know.

00:03:40.238 --> 00:03:41.820
(audience laughs)

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.908
I hate that.

00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:46.130
(audience laughs)

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:49.470
(door opens)
(door slams)

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.267
- Guys, there is somebody
I'd like you to meet.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.325
(monkey mumbling)

00:03:53.325 --> 00:03:54.575
- [Friends] Aw!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.083
- Wait, wait, what is that?

00:03:57.083 --> 00:03:58.750
- That would be Marcel.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.267
You wanna say hi?
- No, no, I don't.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.230
- You know, he's moved on.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.483
Hey, that's the way it goes, right?

00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:07.690
(Marcel tapping)

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:08.523
- Oh my God.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.568
- What?

00:04:10.568 --> 00:04:13.151
(upbeat music)

00:04:14.352 --> 00:04:16.980
- No, no no no, I'm not
saying you're not talented.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.430
You're very talented.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.400
It's just that with the bird dead and all,

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.853
there's very little act left.

00:04:21.853 --> 00:04:22.686
(audience laughs)

00:04:22.686 --> 00:04:24.260
Joey, it's Estelle.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.093
- Hey.

00:04:25.093 --> 00:04:27.810
- [Estelle] So, how did
your audition go today.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.780
- What audition?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.170
- The one I told you about last week.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.620
- What, you need said
anything about an audition.

00:04:34.516 --> 00:04:37.130
(audience laughs)

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.820
- Let me start over.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.076
I just got a call about an audition.

00:04:41.076 --> 00:04:42.500
(audience laughs)

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.370
I think you can still make it.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.660
It's down at the Esther Theater

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.420
and you need to have a monologue prepared.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.492
- Kitty kitty kitty.

00:04:49.492 --> 00:04:52.103
Come here, kitty kitty
kitty kitty kitty kitty,

00:04:52.946 --> 00:04:53.779
kitty,

00:04:53.779 --> 00:04:55.230
kitty,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.800
kitty...

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.127
Hi.

00:04:58.127 --> 00:04:59.210
- Buona sera.

00:05:00.226 --> 00:05:01.348
- Wow.

00:05:01.348 --> 00:05:02.669
- Buongiorno a tutti.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:05.367
(audience laughs)
- Ew!

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:06.402
- Oh.

00:05:06.402 --> 00:05:08.430
- Ross!
- Hey ho.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.263
Ah ha.

00:05:09.263 --> 00:05:10.148
What a.

00:05:10.148 --> 00:05:13.317
(audience laughs)

00:05:13.317 --> 00:05:14.480
What are you doing here?

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.912
- I do Raquel.
- Ah.

00:05:15.912 --> 00:05:18.185
(audience laughs)

00:05:18.185 --> 00:05:19.270
(Bobby knocking)

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.253
- Everybody, it's Fun Bobby!

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.967
- [Everybody] Fun Bobby!

00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:24.430
- Hey Bobby!

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:25.710
- Hey, sorry I'm late,

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:29.850
but my grandfather died
about two hours ago.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.213
But I couldn't get a flight
out 'til tomorrow, so,

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.353
here I am.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.940
- [Monica] Hi, I'll be
ready in just a second.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.700
- Can I talk to you a minute?

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.533
- [Monica] Sure.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.150
- Look, I am just not strong enough

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.750
to be in a codependent
relationship right now, okay?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.209
- Oh shoot.

00:05:49.209 --> 00:05:52.200
(audience laughs)

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.350
- Well, anyway, I hope we can be friends.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.183
- Okay.

00:05:57.138 --> 00:05:59.670
(lips smack)

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.750
Take care.
- Okay, you too.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:02.583
- Bye.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.750
There's nothing to tell, it's
just some guy I work with.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:07.860
- Come on.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.100
You're going out with the guy,

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.718
there's gotta be something wrong with him.

00:06:10.718 --> 00:06:12.046
(audience laughs)

00:06:12.046 --> 00:06:13.837
- So, does he have a hump,
a hump and a hairpiece?

00:06:13.837 --> 00:06:16.180
(audience laughs)

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.874
- Wait, does he eat chalk?

00:06:17.874 --> 00:06:18.810
(audience laughs)

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.220
Just 'cause I don't want her to go through

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.246
what I went through with Carl, ah.

00:06:22.246 --> 00:06:23.970
(audience laughs)
- Okay, everybody relax.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.100
This is not even a date.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.660
It's just two people going out to dinner

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.480
and not having sex.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.651
- Sounds like a date to me.

00:06:29.651 --> 00:06:31.256
(audience laughs)

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:34.200
(gentle music)

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.061
- Hi.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.321
(audience laughs)

00:06:37.321 --> 00:06:39.119
- This guy says hello,
I wanna kill myself.

00:06:39.119 --> 00:06:40.770
(audience laughs)

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:41.920
- Are you okay, sweetie?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.880
- I just feel like someone
reached down my throat,

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.680
grabbed my small intestine,
pulled it out of my mouth,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.250
and tide it around my neck.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:49.336
- Cookie?

00:06:49.336 --> 00:06:51.760
(audience laughs)

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.388
- Carol moved her stuff out today.

00:06:53.388 --> 00:06:54.390
- [Everybody] Oh.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:55.400
- Let me get you some coffee.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.233
- Thanks.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.450
- Ohh, oh.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.295
- No, no, don't, stop cleansing my aura.

00:07:04.295 --> 00:07:05.128
(audience laughs)

00:07:05.128 --> 00:07:07.120
- Come on, you're single,
have some hormone.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.380
- See, but I don't want
to be single, okay?

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.933
I just wanna be married again.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.985
(audience laughs)

00:07:16.985 --> 00:07:18.893
- And I just want a million dollars.

00:07:18.893 --> 00:07:21.350
(audience laughs)

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:22.550
- Rachel?

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:25.420
- Oh God, Monica, hi, thank God.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.070
I just went to your building
and you weren't there

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.550
and then this guy with a big hammer

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.180
said that you might be
here, and you are, you are.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.880
- Can I get you some coffee?

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.360
- Decaf.
(audience laughs)

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.920
Okay, everybody, this is Rachel,

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.550
another Lincoln High survivor.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:40.383
This is everybody.

00:07:40.383 --> 00:07:42.830
This is Chandler, and Phoebe, and Joey.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.570
And you remember my brother Ross?

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:45.556
- Sure.

00:07:45.556 --> 00:07:46.389
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:47.222
Oh!

00:07:47.222 --> 00:07:50.055
(audience laughs)

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:52.493
- Wow.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:55.673
- I know.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.323
It seems smaller somehow.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.248
- Has it always been purple?

00:08:03.248 --> 00:08:06.850
(audience laughs)

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:09.030
- Look around, you guys.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.593
This was your first home.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.730
And it was a happy place.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.313
Filled with love and laughter.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.470
But more important,
because of rent control,

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.975
it was a freaking steal.

00:08:21.975 --> 00:08:24.808
(audience laughs)

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:29.980
- Hey, do you realize that
at one time or another,

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.593
we all lived in this apartment?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.490
- [Rachel] Oh yeah, that's true.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.476
- Oh, I haven't.

00:08:36.476 --> 00:08:38.500
(audience laughs)

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.180
- What about that summer during college

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.630
that you lived with grandma

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.803
and you tried to make it as a dancer?

00:08:43.803 --> 00:08:46.636
(audience laughs)

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:51.330
- Do you realize we
almost made it 10 years

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.489
without that coming up?

00:08:52.489 --> 00:08:55.980
(audience laughs)

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.570
- Oh honey, I forgot.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.590
I promised Treeger that
we'd leave our keys.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.979
- Oh okay.

00:09:00.979 --> 00:09:04.576
(boots stomping softly)

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:06.909
(keys thud)

00:09:16.248 --> 00:09:19.081
(audience laughs)

00:09:25.348 --> 00:09:28.015
(keys clinking)

00:09:35.031 --> 00:09:35.864
(Joey sighs)

00:09:35.864 --> 00:09:37.580
- So I guess this is it.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.413
- Yeah.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.533
I guess so.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.116
- This is harder than
I thought it would be.

00:09:47.116 --> 00:09:49.116
- Oh it's gonna be okay.

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:52.967
Come on.

00:09:54.421 --> 00:09:57.588
(everybody sniffling)

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:02.470
- Do you guys have to go
to the new house right away

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.743
or do you have some time? (sniffles)

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:08.760
- We have some time.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:12.045
- Okay, should we get some coffee?

00:10:12.045 --> 00:10:12.878
- Sure.

00:10:15.048 --> 00:10:15.881
Where?

00:10:15.881 --> 00:10:18.714
(audience laughs)

00:10:20.289 --> 00:10:22.872
(gentle music)

